As far as Thatcherism was concerned that consensus[,] real or imagined, was identified inextricably[ with] the politics of the post-war settlement which was seen as the root cause of all current ills, needing to be radically altered. In order to effect this in a cultural form Thatcherism set out to[ generate] a set[ of affirmative] images based upon the selective revival of particular symbols[ of] person and nation, constructed[ specifically] from stories of war and the interwar period, with an emphasis[ on] the re-legitimation[ of] �[�]van[ished]’(or were they ‘varnished’?) values.
